% Refinement-sort machinery (TODO_0011 rung 1) — membership as PROVABLE facts.
%
% Sorts are EXTRINSIC refinements (Lovas–Pfenning): one content-addressed
% term may inhabit many sorts; membership is a judgment, erased at runtime.
% A subsort declaration `A <: B.` is sugar for a persistent sedge fact
% (synthesized by the loader); the order the checker enforces is its
% reflexive-transitive closure. That closure is MATERIALIZED at load: the
% loader computes it once (the one-time deduction) and injects each pair
% as an ordinary ground `subsort A B` fact, so in-logic premises like
% `!subsort X resource` are answered totally by fact lookup — no recursive
% closure clause, hence no committed-choice completeness caveat. The
% engine's sort DAG (lib/engine/sorts.js) is the same closure as a
% compiled index; the fuzz suite keeps table, facts, and independent
% reachability in agreement.
%
% Importing this file is the opt-in: a calculus without it has no sort
% machinery (absent, not disabled). Programs contribute the facts:
% `bin <: q.` beside the numeric prelude, `wood: resource.` classifiers
% in game files. ILL stays sortless.

sort: type.                                % the classifier of sort names

sedge:   (a: sort) -> (b: sort) -> type.   % declared subsort edge
subsort: (a: sort) -> (b: sort) -> type.   % subsort order (materialized closure)

subsort/refl: subsort S S.
